class RPPController(Node):
    """
    Generic straight-segment precision controller.

    The desired PX4 rover heading is encoded by the horizontal velocity
    vector. No yaw or yaw-rate command is used.

    Mission behavior:
      - Use the first generated 50 mm pass-through points of each new
        segment as a moving line-entry alignment zone.
      - Align while moving continuously; no yaw-rate-only PX4 command.
      - Use deadband-aware line recovery only when large cross-track error
        remains but the PX4 heading request falls below the measured
        drivetrain turning threshold.
      - Release to normal tracking when the rover follows the corrected
        line-capture guidance within 3 degrees and cross-track is <=0.04 m.
      - For the first marking point, lock one fixed C->P1 line from the
        mission-enable rover position to the exact P1 coordinate.
      - Perform segment-entry alignment before high-speed travel
        with a 0.08 m/s velocity-vector command.
      - Enter terminal marking alignment only inside 0.30 m from the
        exact marking coordinate measured from the current rover position.
      - When true geometric guidance error is >=15 degrees, latch a fixed
        60 degree PX4-native pivot request in the same turn direction.
        Release it only when the true geometric bearing is within 3 degrees.
      - Never manufacture a moving current-yaw-relative correction during
        translation; all driving uses a fixed geometric line bearing.
      - Inside 0.30 m, terminal translation follows the smooth
        0.140 m/s to 0.120 m/s distance profile.
      - Below 0.15 m, after the 15 mm / 3 degree gate is valid, drive
        straight on the fixed incoming bearing at 0.120 m/s continuously.
        No pulse method and no yaw-rate-only command are used.
      - Permit terminal marking handoff inside 0.25 m only after the rover
        is forward-facing and inside the 40 mm incoming-line corridor.
      - Use moving forward-heading recovery so PX4 cannot satisfy a large
        heading error by driving the differential rover in reverse.
      - Follow generated 50 mm pass-through points.
      - Use the exact next CSV marking waypoint as the segment goal.
      - After segment alignment, accelerate smoothly to 0.40 m/s.
      - Follow generated 50 mm pass-through points at up to 0.40 m/s.
      - Follow the requested smooth distance-speed test profile:
        0.70m=0.400m/s, 0.60m=0.356m/s, 0.50m=0.260m/s,
        0.40m=0.164m/s, 0.30m=0.140m/s.
      - Enter the terminal marking branch only inside 0.30 m.
      - Smoothly reduce from 0.140 m/s at 0.30 m to 0.120 m/s
        at 0.15 m, then hold continuous 0.120 m/s final creep.
      - Stop only after the measured marking distance is <= 0.03 m.
      - Allow the mission manager to hold for
        three continuous seconds.
      - Enter safe hold immediately after a missed marking capture.

    There is no A/A1 approach-point logic.
    """

